  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Power Tunisia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Tunisia):  Tunisia faces significant challenges in the energy sector.  To tackle them, the Government of Tunisia adopted an energy transition framework for 2030 based on the following priority areas: 1) development of national hydrocarbon resources; 2) strengthening the refining, transporting, and distributing of petroleum products; 3) development of electricity production and strengthening electricity interconnections with different countries; and 4) integration of 30 percent renewable energy by 2030 and reducing the demand for primary energy, which consists of unconverted or original fuels, by 30 percent using energy efficiency techniques. .Through Power Tunisia, USAID will assist Tunisia in meeting the fourth priority by working with the private sector and other key stakeholders to explore ways to achieve the government&apos;s renewable energy and energy efficiency goals..Power Tunisia focuses on diversifying and securing the energy supply while fostering innovation through advanced technology pilots and strategic partnerships. To achieve these objectives, Power Tunisia provides targeted technical assistance, including consulting services, in-kind support, and incentive-based financing (grants), to key stakeholders working to increase the adoption of renewable energy and energy efficiency technologies. Key partners and program counterparts include energy consumers, energy project developers, financial intermediaries (commercial banks, microfinance institutions, and investor organizations), local associations, non-governmental organizations (NGOs), and the international donor community, including multilateral and bilateral development banks and other donors..Power Tunisia will help Tunisia increase renewable energy deployment by 70 megawatts, reduce CO2 Emissions by 100,000 metric tons per year, support over 1,750 Tunisian companies, and mobilize $70 million in clean energy investments..</narrative>
  </description>
